WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:25.714
Type III covers low-pressure chillers. These are commercial systems — big
equipment, big consequences.

00:00:25.714 --> 00:00:51.429
Type III recovery requirements: systems under 200 lbs recover to 0 psig. Systems
200 lbs or more recover to 25 mm Hg absolute. These levels are different from
Type II because low-pressure systems operate differently. Recovery from

00:00:51.429 --> 00:01:17.143
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:42.857
25 mm Hg Absolute: Recovery target for low-pressure systems 200 lbs or more.
Measured in absolute pressure.

00:01:42.857 --> 00:02:08.571
Here's why this matters on the job: Low-pressure recovery requires patience and
proper technique.

00:02:08.571 --> 00:02:34.286
Watch out for these: Under 200 lbs = 0 psig. And — Over 200 lbs = 25 mm Hg
absolute

00:02:34.286 --> 00:03:00.000
Why does a low-pressure system have air leaking in rather than refrigerant
leaking out? Think about the pressure relationship.

